{
 "about": "Skins for cardrig.py: which drawn card each bone wears, with its sockets in card px. A at the joint nearer the body, B at the far joint. Sockets were placed by eye on a 2x grid (critic reg sheets, 2026-10-21), except the poet's, which come from weave/assets/assets.json and sit on her drawn brads. 'cm' is the 3D length the card's A->B is scaled to, so cards cut at six different scales come out on one body. 'w' is the drawn width the card is held to, across its bone: some cards are fat ovals (the man's thigh card, scaled to 44cm long, came out 36cm wide). The man's boot.front/back cards are drawn on square cardboard tiles, so a foot pointing at the camera uses the side card foreshortened instead.",
